course: dictionary
lesson: 14787
title: Publication
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A publication is something that has been printed, or made public, so that people can read it. Books, magazines, newspapers and reports are all publications.
explain: The word comes from the verb publish, which means to print something and make it available to people. «The school's class publication comes out every term.» Here the publication is the printed newsletter that the pupils can read.
explain: Publication can also mean the act of making something known to everyone. «The publication of the results told the whole town what the scientists had found.» Here it means the sharing, not the printed thing itself.
fact: Publication is a noun: a publication, publications.
fact: «Publication» can mean a book, magazine, newspaper or report that has been published.
fact: «Publication» can also mean the act of printing and making something available to people.
fact: «Date of publication» means the day something was first made available to the public.
fact: Publication can be countable (a publication, two publications) or uncountable (the publication of news).
exercise: «The school's class publication comes out every term.» What is a class publication here? | A playground game | *A newsletter that is printed for pupils to read | A kind of maths test | A pencil case
exercise: «The scientists shared their findings by publication in a journal.» What does publication mean in this sentence? | Measuring the size of a page | Hiding the results from everyone | Counting the results | *Making the results known to the public through print
exercise: What is the date of publication of a book? | The day it was lost | The day it was bought from the shop | The day the author started writing it | *The day it was first made available to the public
test: «This weekly publication has a new comic every Monday.» What is a weekly publication? | *A magazine or paper that comes out once a week | A school trip that happens every week | A book written in one week | A test held on Mondays
test: Which of these is a publication? | A cloud in the sky | A wobbly chair | A pencil with no point | *A newspaper that is printed and sold
exam: Which sentence uses publication to mean the act of making news known? | «The dog had a publication in the garden.» | «I ate my publication at lunch.» | *«The publication of the news surprised the whole town.» | «The bus went past the publication.»
